  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want one call that tells me what is new (unread MPs, flagged topics with news), so that the Home screen and background checks share one polite request path.\n\n### Scope\n\n`CheckUpdatesFlow`: MP unread count (LOT-047) + flags page `owntopic=1` (LOT-024 parser) → `UpdateSummary` (unread MPs, flagged topics with a newer last post). Never GETs a topic page (an authenticated topic GET moves flags, E25). At most two requests; reports logged-out/unknown as 'no information', never as proof of expiry (LOT-047 rule).\n\n- Module: HFRClient · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-005 (#149), FEAT-001 (#145)\n- Absorbs: FEATURES.md FEAT-005 'new check updates flow (HFRClient)'\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `MPBackgroundService.swift:70-136` (MP count), `ObjCFavoritesLoaderWorker.m:46-48` (flags page)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-092-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-047 (#73, done)\n- LOT-024 (#52, done)\n- LOT-037 (#64, done)\n- LOT-045 (#71, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\ncaptures #168 and CAP-N5 (#173) (answer shapes of an expired session on the home and flags pages) must exist before the flow classifies them (LESSONS 35-36); LOT-037 classifies a `.hop` answer, LOT-024 alone does not. The flags-page state of #109 (logged-in `forum1f.php?owntopic=1` with no flagged topic) is also listed under \"Captures needed\". All three are open; every dependency above is done.\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-005 (#149), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-091 (#183), LOT-141 (#231); the last lot (LOT-141 (#231)) closes #149.\n- Implements FEAT-001 (#145), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-090 (#182), LOT-143 (#233), LOT-144 (#234); the last lot (LOT-144 (#234)) closes #145.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- #168\n- #109\n- CAP-N5 (#173): Flags page (`owntopic=1`) seen by a session whose cookies expired: list, `.hop` page or login wall?\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] No topic-page request in any path (test with a mock transport that fails on `forum2.php`/`sujet_`).\n- [ ] Logged-out, `.hop` and unreadable answers map to typed outcomes; none is reported as zero news.\n- [ ] Cancellation stops after the current request and returns nothing partial.\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-092-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
